With --split-mode tensor a model's weights loaded far slower than split by
layer, also after 0010 gathered the rows (Qwen3-235B Q4_K_M over four MI250X
GCDs 352 s cold against 113 s by layer, Qwen3-Coder-480B over eight 569 s
against 113, c11-placement load-*, 20-10-2026). Two causes in the way a
weight reached the devices. The meta buffer has no events or host buffers, so
the loader gave it no async uploads: each weight read into memory was read
whole, then copied, the file idle during the copy and the devices idle during
the read. And the meta buffer copied a weight to its devices one after the
other, from one thread, though each device has its own link to the host.

Now the loader reads the next weight while the last one is copied, for a
meta buffer (two weights in memory at most; LLAMA_LOAD_OVERLAP=0 reads and
copies in turn), and logs how long reading, copying and waiting took. The meta
buffer copies a weight of 16 MiB or more to each device on a thread of its own
(GGML_META_SET_THREADS=0 copies one device after the other).

